From bafe0cafc97bc5b9c7f58fb0c476ab3bb86f66f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:36:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] chore(fonts): drop THEBOLDFONT (licence unverifiable);
 alias it to Montserrat-Black

Sanji's ruling 2026-11-18: THEBOLDFONT.ttf is UNVERIFIED in FONT_MANIFEST
(no provable licence), so it ships in nothing.

- backend/fonts/THEBOLDFONT.ttf removed, and its manifest entry; check_fonts
  now passes on the real folder (34 fonts, all OFL-1.1 / Apache-2.0).
- font_registry.FONT_ALIASES: the name THEBOLDFONT resolves to
  Montserrat-Black (OFL, verified, closest heavy geometric face already
  bundled), so stored editor drafts (CaptionStyle.font Literal unchanged),
  AI-edit plans and old templates still render.
- The four templates that named it (mrbeast, neon, large_centre_pop,
  bold_uppercase) now name Montserrat-Black directly.
- fetch_fonts.py no longer lists it among existing fonts.

Test pins updated (deliberate product change, reasons inline):
- test_font_manifest: 34 entries, no UNVERIFIED, check_fonts clean; /fonts >= 34.
- test_caption_glyph_fallback: the fallback tests simulate the dropped
  font's ASCII-only coverage for the aliased file; fallback text keeps its
  own case (the caps-only rule belonged to the dropped file); the cmap test
  uses Bangers (no Cyrillic); new test: the dropped name resolves.
- test_video_utils_effects: internal-family example is TikTokSans-Bold.
Verified: those files + font_registry/fontsdir/font deletion + transition
API: 33 passed, 1 skipped (fontconfig absent on Windows). Pre-existing on
e632d3e too: test_caption_width x3, test_reference_style_look_stage2 x1,
test_burn_ass_subtitles_passes_selected_fonts_dir (Windows libass/paths).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
