+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@ What changed in SnipNova for people using the product. Newest dates are first.
 Add a line here when a pull request changes something a user can see. Use **New**, **Improved**, **Fixed**, or **Under the hood**, describe the change in plain language, and link the pull request. Skip internal-only work, or fold it into one **Under the hood** line. Do not include customer names, email addresses, user IDs, or anything else private.
 
 ## 2026-11-18
+- **Changed:** The "The Bold Font" caption face is no longer bundled because its licence could not be verified. The MrBeast, Neon, Large Centre Pop and Bold Uppercase caption styles now use Montserrat Black, and drafts or styles that named the old font render in Montserrat Black automatically. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
 - **Improved:** When a clip shows a screen that matters (a stage screen announcing nominees, a monitor, a meme on a window), the screen is now shown readable on top with the person reacting below, instead of being cropped away or shown tiny. The rest of the clip keeps one calm full-frame layout, so the layout only changes when the screen comes on and goes off. Off until approved: set `SCREEN_SUBJECT=on` to try it. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
 - **Improved:** Clip picking can now see moments that happen in the picture, not only in the words: an award walk-up, a speech with burned-in subtitles, a celebration. These moments are offered to the AI picker, and a clip that ends just as one starts now keeps going until it finishes (within the 60-second limit). Off until approved: set `SELECTION_EVENTS=on` and `CLIP_CAP_KEEP_VISUAL_TAIL=on` to try it. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
 - **Fixed:** Captions no longer repeat a phrase over and over when the speech recogniser loops over loud crowd or music noise; the phrase is shown once. Caption lines now follow the phrasing of the speech (sentence ends, pauses, commas) and never leave a single word stranded on its own line. Off until approved: set `CAPTION_LOOP_FILTER=on` and `CAPTION_PHRASE_SPLIT=on` to try it. ([#TBD](https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip/pulls))
